        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "For developing optical lattice clocks to unprecedented precision."
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B032",
    "B006"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "I change my preference from B032 to B008. Optical lattice clocks are a precise, reproducible advance in atomic physics, and their measurement capability can test fundamental physics as well as improve timekeeping. This is a well-defined achievement with two shortlisted contributors whose work can be credited together.",
    "case_against": "The central question is whether precision and broad utility amount to a fundamental discovery of Nobel scale. The case would be stronger if the record established specific new physical results enabled by this precision, rather than resting chiefly on the capability itself.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "You prefer B040 partly because its citation centers on one theory and prediction, whereas B032 joins the distinct histories of the Aharonov–Bohm effect and Berry phase.",
        "response": "That distinction has changed my assessment. B032 expresses an important shared lesson about quantum phase, but joining the two histories makes the public claim and attribution less coherent. B008 offers a more bounded achievement and a clearer pairing of credited contributors."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "You regard optical lattice clocks as exceptionally mature, while asking whether precision measurement carries enough fundamental weight relative to its broad utility.",
        "response": "I share that concern. Precision alone is not the full scientific case; the clocks matter here because they can serve as stringent tests of fundamental physics. I favor B008 if the committee can make that scientific reach central to the citation, while recognizing that the evidence for particular enabled discoveries remains an uncertainty."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Which fundamental tests or results enabled by optical lattice clock precision should anchor the prize case.",
      "The historical contributions that justify the proposed credit to Katori and Ye."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
